* On being an Artist
To be or not to be an artist, this question has bothered me
since I started wondering what I wanted to for a living. I
always were under the impression that artists struggle to
make money, but at the same time true unparalleled skill was
rewarded greatly.
Experience has nothing but confirmed my
bias to a certain degree, on one side art will /never/ be a
basic necessity good like food or water. On a third world
country like mine it's unthinkable someone would prioritize
getting a painting or going to a concert over providing to
their family. They're already struggling to make ends meet,
adding further load either by being an art elitist or using
the police power of the state to enforce "rights", that
provide mediocre artists with the sufficient funding at the
expense of the hard work of the commonfolk it's something I
would never agree or like to be part of.
But on the other side, quite literally the other side of the
world, look at the most succesfull stablished mangakas like
村田雄介(Murata Yusuke); Boichi; illustrators like さいとう
なおき(Saito Naoki) or even tangentially related to
drawing/painting; the writer 西尾維新(Nisio Isin).
Having stablished both sides of the spectrum it would be
logical to think that here there's just not a market for
such and such type of artistic endeavors. But there actually
IS examples of succesfull artists that had interesting
carreers despite the day to day struggle of living in Argentina.
